report='''# Historical evidence supplement

Recovered 30 original files within the new allocation, without modifying the previous audit or original evidence. No models, solvers, benchmarks, graders or builds ran.

All 23 original Requests provider result receipts are now inspected: 7 for cold-v1 and 16 for cold-v2. Every record reports one attempted POST, HTTP 200, remote usage known and a terminal response. Original raw counters match normalized counters and prior per-event projections. Separate cohort sums remain 108,981 and 243,255 tokens; no trajectory completes. Sixteen cold-v2 receipt hashes match their original fixed-cohort report commitments. Cold-v1 original aggregate per-receipt hash bindings were not re-read within this 30-file allocation.

The records report grok-4.6 and fingerprint fp_e41c6060b2628547. A provider fingerprint is not independently authenticated model weights. These are 23 single-request call identities, not 23 inferred conversation sessions. The original wrapper says “provider total; components preserved without assuming disjointness.” In every recovered record, the observed arithmetic is input+visible output+reasoning=total; cached input stays a subset. This remains separate from Codex and Grok CLI schemas. Per-request API charges are original reported observations, not settlement or inferred token pricing. Credential metadata and model text are excluded from exports.

The original compositional result now supplies cvc5 1.3.3 and independent Z3 4.15.4 with QF_LIA interpolation and source-artifact validation. Its 242 loaded path/hash entries cover only files under the supplied native source root: the recorder's own source explicitly filters sys.modules by that root. This partially closes import provenance, not full standard-library/third-party/solver binary closure. No imported implementation bytes, solver binaries or semantic theorem were independently reexecuted here. Internal benchmark estimates remain excluded from efficiency claims.

Both archive-consumption summaries are recovered directly. The constructed controller archive records 4 accepted events, 5 units each, 7 rejected controls, one honest proof and one pairing verification; its driver takes 14.749495 seconds. The actual Requests accepted-source archive records 1 event, 4 units, 97 restored files, 8 rejected controls and one honest proof/pairing; its driver takes 14.737743 seconds. Original execution truth remains false as a claim of these proofs, fresh grader calls are 0 and production admission is false. Nested phase timers are not added. The repository control named cyclic_parent remains a recorded rejection; the prior report says earlier kind/lookup rejection occurred, not verified cycle traversal.

The signed-procedure original summary records 136 distinct TEST interpreter invocations: 13 true and 123 false computed answers, all equal their recorded expected decisions. Thirteen explicit runtime controls pass. The 816 dispatches and 2,184 admission events are repeated internal steps/gates, not repair trials or independent candidates. Worker clocks sum 17.242940 seconds, with 1.402121 seconds preparation separately recorded. No model calls, registry promotion or production authority are reported. This remains a bounded arithmetic procedure under trusted development custody, not repository-repair generalization.

The companion ledgers contain allowlisted status/count/hash/identity fields only. Original archives, keys, certificates and full statement correspondence were not revalidated. Historical reuse_analysis.json recovery remains unchanged because the 30-file allocation was used on the named priority gaps. No absence is treated as proof that a historical experiment did not occur.
'''
